   team_id \tab integer \tab Unique NBA Stats team identifier. \cr
   team_name \tab character \tab Full team display name. \cr
   team_tricode \tab character \tab Three-letter team code. \cr
   side \tab character \tab Whether the team was 'home' or 'away'. \cr
   minutes \tab character \tab Total minutes played, as an \code{MM:SS} string. \cr
   field_goals_made \tab integer \tab Field goals made. \cr
   field_goals_attempted \tab integer \tab Field goal attempts. \cr
   field_goals_percentage \tab numeric \tab Field goal percentage (0-1). \cr
   three_pointers_made \tab integer \tab Three-point field goals made. \cr
   three_pointers_attempted \tab integer \tab Three-point field goal attempts. \cr
   three_pointers_percentage \tab numeric \tab Three-point field goal percentage (0-1). \cr
   free_throws_made \tab integer \tab Free throws made. \cr
   free_throws_attempted \tab integer \tab Free throw attempts. \cr
   free_throws_percentage \tab numeric \tab Free throw percentage (0-1). \cr
   rebounds_offensive \tab integer \tab Offensive rebounds. \cr
   rebounds_defensive \tab integer \tab Defensive rebounds. \cr
   rebounds_total \tab integer \tab Total rebounds. \cr
   assists \tab integer \tab Assists. \cr
   steals \tab integer \tab Steals. \cr
   blocks \tab integer \tab Blocks. \cr
   turnovers \tab integer \tab Turnovers. \cr
   fouls_personal \tab integer \tab Personal fouls. \cr
   points \tab integer \tab Points scored. \cr
   plus_minus_points \tab numeric \tab Plus/minus point differential. \cr
   game_id \tab character \tab Unique game identifier. \cr
   season \tab integer \tab Season identifier (4-digit year, END year of the season). \cr
}

Returns a \code{hoopR_data} tibble of team season stats (178 columns:
rank fields plus standard/rank box-score rate/counting stats for the
season). See \code{names(load_nba_stats_team_season_stats())} for the full
column set, or the \code{team_stats_base} table of
\code{\link[=load_nba_stats_leaguedash]{load_nba_stats_leaguedash()}} for the equivalent parameter-cube asset.
}
\description{
Loads season-level NBA coaching staff data scraped from the
NBA Stats API. One row per coach-team-season triple. Backed by the
\code{hoopR-nba-stats-data} pipeline that reads raw JSONs from
\code{hoopR-nba-stats-raw} and publishes csv/parquet/rds artifacts to the
\code{nba_stats_coaches} release tag.

Loads season-level NBA draft picks scraped from the NBA
Stats API (\code{drafthistory}-style outputs). One row per pick. Backed by
the \code{hoopR-nba-stats-data} pipeline that reads raw JSONs from
\code{hoopR-nba-stats-raw} and publishes csv/parquet/rds artifacts to the
\code{nba_stats_draft} release tag.

Loads the per-event 10-man on-court lineup (5 home + 5 away)
scraped alongside the NBA Stats API play-by-play feed. One row per
play-by-play action, with each player slot's NBA Stats person id. Backed
by the \code{hoopR-nba-stats-data} pipeline that publishes csv.gz/parquet/rds
artifacts to the \code{nba_stats_game_lineups} release tag.

Loads the per-game \strong{inactive player} list scraped from the
NBA Stats API -- the \code{InactivePlayers} result set of
\code{boxscoresummaryv2}. One row per inactive athlete-game pair, not a full
per-game roster: use \code{\link[=load_nba_stats_player_game_logs]{load_nba_stats_player_game_logs()}} for the
athletes who did play. Backed by the \code{hoopR-nba-stats-data} pipeline
that publishes csv/parquet/rds artifacts to the \code{nba_stats_game_rosters}
release tag.

Loads season-level 5-man on-court lineup statistics
(\code{leaguedashlineups}-style outputs, \code{Base} measure). Backed by the
\code{hoopR-nba-stats-data} pipeline that publishes csv/parquet/rds artifacts
to the \code{nba_stats_lineups} release tag. For \code{Advanced}/\code{Misc}/\code{Scoring}/
\code{Opponent}/\verb{Four Factors} measures and 2/3/4-man groupings, use
\code{\link[=load_nba_stats_leaguedash]{load_nba_stats_leaguedash()}} with \code{table = "lineups_*"}.

Loads game-level officials data scraped from the NBA Stats
API (\code{boxscoresummaryv2}-style outputs). One row per official-game pair.
Backed by the \code{hoopR-nba-stats-data} pipeline that publishes
csv/parquet/rds artifacts to the \code{nba_stats_officials} release tag.

Loads season-level NBA play-by-play scraped from the NBA
Stats API modern game-feed. One row per play-by-play action, with shot
location, on/off-court lineup joins available via
\code{\link[=load_nba_stats_game_lineups]{load_nba_stats_game_lineups()}}. Backed by the \code{hoopR-nba-stats-data}
pipeline that publishes csv.gz/parquet/rds artifacts to the
\code{nba_stats_pbp} release tag.

Loads per-player per-game box scores scraped from the NBA
Stats API \code{boxscoretraditionalv3}-style output. One row per
athlete-game pair. Backed by the \code{hoopR-nba-stats-data} pipeline that
publishes csv/parquet/rds artifacts to the \code{nba_stats_player_boxscores}
release tag.

Loads per-player per-game logs scraped from
\code{stats.nba.com/leaguegamelog?PlayerOrTeam=P} (one row per
athlete-game pair: minutes, shooting splits, rebounds, steals, blocks,
turnovers, personal fouls, plus/minus). Backed by the
\code{hoopR-nba-stats-data} pipeline that publishes csv/parquet/rds
artifacts to the \code{nba_stats_player_game_logs} release tag.

Loads season-level NBA player statistics
(\code{leaguedashplayerstats}-style outputs, \code{Base} measure). Backed by the
\code{hoopR-nba-stats-data} pipeline that publishes csv/parquet/rds
artifacts to the \code{nba_stats_player_season_stats} release tag. For
\code{Advanced}/\code{Misc}/\code{Scoring}/\code{Usage}/\code{Defense} measures and player
tracking (drives, passing, touches, speed/distance, etc.), use
\code{\link[=load_nba_stats_leaguedash]{load_nba_stats_leaguedash()}} with \code{table = "player_stats_*"} or
\code{table = "player_tracking_*"}.

Loads possession-level data derived from the NBA Stats API
play-by-play -- one row per possession, with the on-court 5-man
lineups for both teams, shooting/rebounding/turnover splits, and the
possession start type. Backed by the \code{hoopR-nba-stats-data} pipeline
that publishes csv.gz/parquet/rds artifacts to the
\code{nba_stats_possessions} release tag.

Loads season-level NBA team rosters scraped from the NBA
Stats API. One row per athlete-team-season triple. Backed by the
\code{hoopR-nba-stats-data} pipeline that publishes csv/parquet/rds
artifacts to the \code{nba_stats_rosters} release tag.

Loads season-level NBA schedules scraped from
\code{stats.nba.com/leaguegamefinder} (regular season + playoffs combined,
pre-rejoined home/away). Backed by the \code{hoopR-nba-stats-data} pipeline
that publishes csv/parquet/rds artifacts to the \code{nba_stats_schedules}
release tag.

Loads shot events scraped from the NBA Stats API. One row
per shot attempt with legacy court coordinates, action/sub type,
distance, and made/missed result, carried through from the play-by-play
feed (not \code{shotchartdetail}). Backed by the \code{hoopR-nba-stats-data}
pipeline that publishes csv/parquet/rds artifacts to the
\code{nba_stats_shots} release tag.

Loads season-level NBA standings (\code{leaguestandingsv3}-style
outputs). One row per team-season. Backed by the \code{hoopR-nba-stats-data}
pipeline that publishes csv/parquet/rds artifacts to the
\code{nba_stats_standings} release tag.

Loads per-team per-game box scores scraped from the NBA
Stats API \code{boxscoretraditionalv3}-style output. One row per team-game
pair. Backed by the \code{hoopR-nba-stats-data} pipeline that publishes
csv/parquet/rds artifacts to the \code{nba_stats_team_boxscores} release tag.

Loads season-level team statistics
(\code{leaguedashteamstats}-style outputs, \code{Base} measure). Backed by the
\code{hoopR-nba-stats-data} pipeline that publishes csv/parquet/rds
artifacts to the \code{nba_stats_team_season_stats} release tag. For
\code{Advanced}/\code{Misc}/\code{Scoring}/\code{Defense}/\code{Opponent}/\verb{Four Factors}
measures, use \code{\link[=load_nba_stats_leaguedash]{load_nba_stats_leaguedash()}} with \code{table = "team_stats_*"}.
}
